    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0797" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.3516/8–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paddock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-26T18:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1948—6
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>51. Closing post Vladivostok<anchor n="2" xml:id="d670-f1"/> will require
                    transmitting messages Dept thru Emb Moscow. Attempt send next tel both routes as
                    test. Emb Moscow advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d670-f1" n="2" xml:id="d670-f1-content">
                <p>For situation leading to the closing of the Consulate General at Vladivostok, see
                    note 156 from the Soviet Embassy, August 24, and the Department of State’s note,
                    September 9, <ref target="frus1948v04">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>
                    </ref>, “Union of Soviet Socialist Republics” (collection 3).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
